  "question": {
    "text": "A real valued function $f(x)$ satisfies the functional equation $f(x-y)=f(x) f(y)-f(a-x)$ $f(a+y)$ where $a$ is a given constant and $f(0)=1, f(2 a-x)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FLcez",
      "text": "\n$-f(x)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "hbr9W",
      "text": "\n$f(x)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sb8iW",
      "text": "\n$f(a)+f(a-x)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "v7ecP",
      "text": "\n$f(-x)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(a-(x-a))=f(a) f(x-a)-f(0) f(x)$\n$=-f(x)\\left[\\because x=0, y=0, f(0)=f^2(0)-f^2(a) \\Rightarrow f^2(a)=0 \\Rightarrow f(a)=0\\right]$.",
    "image": null
  },
